All six features are implemented and verified (17 integration tests pass). Here's what changed:

**`app/auth.py`** — Implemented `require_api_key`: reads `X-API-Key` header, validates against `VALID_API_KEYS`, returns 401 if missing or invalid, returns the username on success.

**`app/main.py`** — Four additions to the existing endpoints:

1. **`GET /tasks`** — Added optional query params `status`, `priority`, `assigned_to` (all combinable) for filtering, plus `page` (default 1, min 1) and `page_size` (default 20, min 1) for pagination. Filtering runs before slicing.

2. **`POST /tasks`** — Requires `require_api_key` via `Depends`. Validates `project_id` exists (404 if not). Auto-generates ID as `max(existing IDs) + 1`. Returns 201 with the created task.

3. **`PUT /tasks/{task_id}`** — Requires auth. Uses `TaskUpdate` (all fields optional) with `model_dump(exclude_unset=True)` so only provided fields are patched. Returns 404 if task not found.

4. **`DELETE /tasks/{task_id}`** — Requires auth. Returns 204 on success, 404 if task not found.
